{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-debug final report\n\nProblem: the release preflight failed deterministically at `test_full_backend_account_is_present` on hosts with scc/lizard installed.\n\nProven root cause: the test asserted a metric coverage record without controlling optional metric-tool availability. Runtime inspection resolved `/opt/homebrew/bin/scc`; the below-threshold fixture yielded no metric match record, so reconstruction omitted the backend (`tests/unit/grounding/test_coverage_reconstruction.py:96-112`; `src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py:336-420`). Forcing tool absence produced the expected `metric/skipped/no_tool` record and ruled out the production reconstruction path.\n\nTest proof: the existing focused node was RED first. A separate held-out behavioral oracle placed a fake installed scc ahead of PATH and ran the node; it was RED at the original assertion before repair, GREEN after the held-out fixer, RED again when the exact fixture-control defect was seeded back, and GREEN after restoration. The committed test asserts observable coverage status/reason; collected=yes, executed=yes, gate=`make test`. Full module: 5 passed.\n\nFix: `test_full_backend_account_is_present` now forces `_METRIC_CANDIDATES` to a missing executable and asserts `skipped >= 1` plus `reason=no_tool`, matching the trusted neighboring contract test. Production semantics are unchanged.\n\nScope and safety: one test file only; no production callers or behavioral dependencies, no new capability or dependency, and no test weakening (three exact assertions were added). `make lint` passed. The external held-out oracle asserts subprocess exit/output and is refactor-resistant at the production boundary.\n\nSiblings: construct sweep across grounding metric tests found their absent-tool cases already control `shutil.which` or metric candidates (`test_conformance.py`, `test_engine_b.py`, `test_non_adoption.py`); no additional host-coupled sibling was confirmed. Parity sweep is N/A because this is a test-fixture invariant, not a multi-channel product surface.\n\nResidual risk: accepted — a present metric tool with zero over-threshold matches emits no match record by current `_metric_invoke` semantics; this repair deliberately preserves that production behavior and makes the test precondition explicit.\n\nReplication: the original focused node and the entire coverage-reconstruction module now pass on the same host that reproduced the release failure."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786059382239198001,"uuid":"0a69c1ec-41f9-40dc-b524-0c39fa20888d"}